  {"SI No":19,"Test Case Name":"pcie_dma_write_test","Test Description":"This test verifies PCIe DMA write and read-back operations across all four DMA channels (0-3) on both PCIE0 and PCIE1 controller instances.","Test Objective":"Verify PCIe DMA write and read-back data transfer across all four DMA channels on both PCIE controller instances.","Test Category":"Functional","Test Steps":"1. Clear the system synchronization register by writing 0x0.\n2. Initiate PCIe link training.\n3. Poll the SII status register at offset 0xC0 until link-up.\n4. Read the TYPE1_DEV_ID_VEND_ID_REG.\n5. Write 0x7 to the TYPE1_STATUS_COMMAND_REG.\n6. Execute BAR programming.\n7. Poll the synchronization register until 0x12345678.\n8. Preload source memory.\n9. Enable GIC interrupts.\n10. Write 0x0 to DMA_WRITE_INT_MASK_OFF.\n11. Write 0x0 to DMA_READ_INT_MASK_OFF.\n12-16. Program and trigger DMA write channels 0-3.\n17-20. Program and trigger DMA read channels 0-3.\n21. Handle interrupts.\n22. Repeat for PCIE1.\n23. Call finish(0).","Expected Results":"All DMA write and read-back transfers complete successfully with interrupt assertion on both PCIE0 and PCIE1.","Register Name":"NA","Register Offset (Hex)":"NA","Register Block":"NA","Block Base Offset (Hex)":"NA","Absolute Register Address (Hex)":"0xE6004100","Fields Accessed":"NA","Bit Range":"NA","Field Width (bits)":"NA","Access Type":"NA","Reset Value":"NA","Read/Write Operation":"write","Values Written":"0x0; polled for 0x12345678","IP_NAME":"PCIE","Source File":"program.c","Macro Name in Code":"0xE6004100","Notes":"System-level synchronization register."},
